{
  "requirement": "Each page has the same result fields as the originating tool. Text reads return\nsuccessive portions of text. Listings, outlines, and searches return successive\narrays of whole entries in their original order. Only a page with a successor\nincludes `next`.\n\nReusing a UUID returns the same page from the original snapshot, including the\nsame successor UUID if more remains. A malformed UUID, an unknown UUID, or a UUID\nfrom another conversation returns a tool error under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.tool_agent.isolation`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests adequately cover `requirements.sdk.graph.validation-context.pages.behavior`.\n\n**Obligations and the tests that cover them**\n\n1. **Pages carry the originating tool's result fields.**\n   - `search_pages_return_every_original_match_in_order` checks `complete`, a UUID `search_id`, `instructions` on the first page only, and each match entry exactly (`node`, `file`, `selector`, `excerpt`, `tag`).\n   - `outline_continuations_keep_the_file_and_complete_ordered_items` checks `node` on every outline page and `file`/`selector` on every read page.\n   - `listing_continuations_return_complete_paths_from_the_original_listing` checks each `files` entry's `node` and `data`.\n   - `source_read_pages_retain_text_and_dependencies_without_another_read` checks `node.selector` on each page.\n\n2. **Text reads return successive portions of text.**\n   - `graph_read_pages_retain_the_prepared_snapshot_after_contents_change` uses multibyte text (`é` repeated 8192 times, then a suffix). It concatenates the page texts and asserts they equal the original.\n   - The root read in `outline_continuations_keep_the_file_and_complete_ordered_items` does the same over three or more pages (800 repeated lines of about 27 bytes each).\n   - `source_read_pages_retain_text_and_dependencies_without_another_read` rejoins the pages and compares them with the original.\n\n3. **Listings, outlines and searches return successive arrays of whole entries in original order.**\n   - Searches: 350 hits over several pages. Entries are compared in order with the expected values and the total count is asserted.\n   - Outlines: 401 items over several pages. Node, file, selector and kind are checked per item, in order.\n   - Listings: 2000 files over several pages. They are compared in order with the expected list, even though a file is added during paging.\n\n4. **Only a page with a successor includes `next`.**\n   - `graph_read_pages_retain_the_prepared_snapshot_after_contents_change` asserts `next` is present exactly on the first of two pages.\n   - The other paging loops stop only when `next` is absent. Together with the `pages > 1` assertions and exact item counts, this ties `next` to the existence of a successor.\n\n5. **Reusing a UUID returns the same page from the original snapshot, with the same successor UUID.**\n   - `search_obligations_follow_delivery_and_keep_the_original_snapshot` rewrites the file after the first search. It fetches the second page, then fetches it again and asserts the text is identical.\n   - The 300 entries span several 8 KiB pages, so the second page has a successor. The identical text therefore includes the same `next`.\n   - The page-reuse code (`Pages::get` and `Pages::retain`) is shared by all tool kinds, so a separate reuse test per kind is not needed.\n   - The other tests also confirm snapshot retention: files are changed after the first page, and later pages still match the original.\n\n6. **Malformed, unknown and cross-conversation UUIDs return a tool error.**\n   - Malformed (`\"invalid\"`) and unknown (an all-zero UUID) are asserted to error in `outline_continuations_keep_the_file_and_complete_ordered_items`.\n   - Another conversation: in `search_obligations_follow_delivery_and_keep_the_original_snapshot`, a peer session's `get_next_page` with the first session's `next` errors.\n   - `graph_page_ids_from_a_populated_peer_conversation_are_rejected` has a populated peer conversation present a foreign page UUID. It asserts an error result containing \"unknown page\".\n   - The `tool_agent.isolation` citation needs no separate coverage.\n\n**Gaps**\n\nNo gaps found. Reuse is asserted only through search pages, but all page kinds share the same retention and lookup code, so this does not leave a distinct scenario untested.",
  "references": "1ac80069e6c37d2808f2a07935fa541926528e3931df8b3a2c423e0fed2a9800",
